# 16. Delivery phases

### Phase A — Workspace foundation
Root tooling, workspaces, apps/headquarter, apps/arsy, packages/types, packages/contract, packages/lint.

### Phase B — ARSY runtime
packages/arsy-core, Fastify application factory, app lifecycle, health, error handling, typed routes.

### Phase C — ORM foundation
packages/orm, model metadata, field registry, model registry, query/domain model, addon loader.

### Phase D — Database and PocketBase
packages/orm-db, packages/orm-db-adaptor, packages/orm-db-adaptor-pocketbase, compatibility matrix, adapter contract tests.

### Phase E — Base addon
packages/orm-addon-base, automatic BaseEntity fields, active state, AuditTrail.

### Phase F — Business addons
packages/orm-addon-project and packages/orm-addon-intelligent.

### Phase G — Headquarter integration
Connect Headquarter to ARSY using packages/contract. Replace demo data only for features that have verified backend endpoints.

### Phase H — Operational hardening
Auth, access control, observability, budgets, kill switch, migration runbook, backup/restore, audit review, deployment docs.

Do not skip ahead by creating a fake ORM facade over direct PocketBase calls. The ORM and adapter boundaries must be real and tested.

# 17. Definition of done

The foundation is accepted only when:
- apps/headquarter exists and is the named frontend.
- apps/arsy starts a Fastify server through packages/arsy-core.
- packages/orm registers declarative models.
- Addon manifests resolve in dependency order.
- orm-addon-base provides id, active, timestamps, actor fields, and central audit behavior without addon duplication.
- orm-addon-project and orm-addon-intelligent depend on base and declare only business-specific fields.
- PocketBase adapter declares and enforces its actual capabilities.
- Unsupported adapter features fail clearly.
- API contracts are shared between Headquarter and ARSY.
- Typecheck, lint, unit tests, and integration tests pass.
- No secret, false integration, simulated sale, or unsupported capability is represented as real.
- Documentation is updated with implementation facts, not aspirational claims.

